Feature: Tempo training
  As a musician using the metronome TUI
  I want the tempo to automatically step toward a target BPM every N measures
  So that I can train up (or down) to a target tempo without manually bumping BPM

  Background:
    Given the metronome app has started

  @ft:16
  Scenario: Enable tempo training
    Given the metronome is playing
    And   the tempo training header reads "Tempo Training: off"
    When  I press "t"
    Then  the tempo training header should read "Tempo Training: on"
    And   the tempo training table should be shown

  @ft:61
  Scenario: Measures elapsed before enabling do not count toward the first interval
    Given the tempo-training interval is 2 measures
    And   the step is 10 BPM
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    And   5 measures have elapsed with tempo training off
    When  I press "t"
    And   1 measure has elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    When  1 more measure has elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"

  @ft:62
  Scenario: Toggling tempo training off and back on restarts the interval
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 2 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    And   1 measure has elapsed
    When  I press "t"
    And   I press "t"
    And   1 measure has elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    When  1 more measure has elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"

  @ft:19
  Scenario: Disable tempo training
    Given tempo training is enabled
    When  I press "t"
    Then  the tempo training header should read "Tempo Training: off"
    And   the tempo training table should not be shown

  @ft:20
  Scenario: Tempo training increases BPM after the configured number of measures
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    When  beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"

  @ft:60
  Scenario: Tempo change is scheduled starting at beat 1 of the next measure, not beat 4
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  7 measures have elapsed
    And   beats 1 through 3 of the 8th measure have been struck
    And   beat 4 of the 8th measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    But   the beat immediately following beat 4 should still be scheduled at 120 BPM
    When  beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"
    Then  the beat immediately following that should be scheduled at 130 BPM

  @ft:22
  Scenario: Tempo training holds once the target BPM is reached
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures and a target of 130
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"
    When  8 more measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 130 BPM"
    And   the tempo training header should read "Tempo Training: target reached (130 bpm)"
    And   the status bar should show "PLAYING"

  @ft:17
  Scenario: Default tempo-training header, table hidden
    Then  the tempo training header should read "Tempo Training: off"
    And   the tempo training table should not be shown

  @ft:53
  Scenario: Tempo-training table shows the default values once enabled
    When  I press "t"
    Then  the tempo training table should be shown
    And   the tempo training table's Step row should read "10 bpm"
    And   the tempo training table's Interval row should read "8 measures"
    And   the tempo training table's Target row should read "180 bpm"
    And   the tempo training table's Start row should read "120 bpm"

  @ft:18
  Scenario: Increase the tempo-training step size
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training step is 2 BPM
    When  I press "]"
    Then  the tempo training table's Step row should read "3 bpm"

  @ft:26
  Scenario: Decrease the tempo-training step size
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training step is 2 BPM
    When  I press "["
    Then  the tempo training table's Step row should read "1 bpm"

  @ft:27
  Scenario: Tempo-training step size cannot go below the minimum
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training step is 1 BPM
    When  I press "["
    Then  the tempo training table's Step row should read "1 bpm"

  @ft:21
  Scenario: Tempo-training step size cannot go above the maximum
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training step is 20 BPM
    When  I press "]"
    Then  the tempo training table's Step row should read "20 bpm"

  @ft:29
  Scenario: Adjusting the step size works while the metronome is stopped
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the metronome is stopped
    And   the tempo-training step is 2 BPM
    When  I press "]"
    Then  the tempo training table's Step row should read "3 bpm"

  @ft:23
  Scenario: Changed step size is used on the next tempo-training increase
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  I press "]"
    And   8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 131 BPM"

  @ft:24
  Scenario: Increase the tempo-training interval
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training interval is 8 measures
    When  I press "}"
    Then  the tempo training table's Interval row should read "9 measures"

  @ft:25
  Scenario: Decrease the tempo-training interval
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training interval is 8 measures
    When  I press "{"
    Then  the tempo training table's Interval row should read "7 measures"

  @ft:33
  Scenario: Tempo-training interval cannot go below the minimum
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training interval is 1 measure
    When  I press "{"
    Then  the tempo training table's Interval row should read "1 measure"

  @ft:34
  Scenario: Tempo-training interval cannot go above the maximum
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training interval is 32 measures
    When  I press "}"
    Then  the tempo training table's Interval row should read "32 measures"

  @ft:28
  Scenario: Adjusting the interval works while the metronome is stopped
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the metronome is stopped
    And   the tempo-training interval is 8 measures
    When  I press "}"
    Then  the tempo training table's Interval row should read "9 measures"

  @ft:36
  Scenario: Changed interval is used for the next tempo-training increase
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  I press "}"
    And   8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    When  1 more measure has elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    When  beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"

  @ft:30
  Scenario: Increase the tempo-training target
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 180 BPM
    When  I press "m"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "181 bpm"

  @ft:31
  Scenario: Decrease the tempo-training target
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 180 BPM
    When  I press "n"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "179 bpm"

  @ft:32
  Scenario: Tempo-training target cannot go below the minimum
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 20 BPM
    When  I press "n"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "20 bpm"

  @ft:40
  Scenario: Tempo-training target cannot go above the maximum
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 300 BPM
    When  I press "m"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "300 bpm"

  @ft:41
  Scenario: Adjusting the target works while the metronome is stopped
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the metronome is stopped
    And   the tempo-training target is 180 BPM
    When  I press "m"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "181 bpm"

  @ft:45
  Scenario: Increase the tempo-training target by a large increment
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 180 BPM
    When  I press "shift+m"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "190 bpm"

  @ft:46
  Scenario: Decrease the tempo-training target by a large increment
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 180 BPM
    When  I press "shift+n"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "170 bpm"

  @ft:47
  Scenario: Tempo-training target cannot go below the minimum with the large increment
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 20 BPM
    When  I press "shift+n"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "20 bpm"

  @ft:48
  Scenario: Tempo-training target cannot go above the maximum with the large increment
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the tempo-training target is 300 BPM
    When  I press "shift+m"
    Then  the tempo training table's Target row should read "300 bpm"

  @ft:35
  Scenario: Tempo training steps BPM downward when the target is below the current BPM
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures and a target of 100
    And   the BPM is 130
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 120 BPM"

  @ft:69
  Scenario: Tempo training holds once BPM steps down to reach the target
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures and a target of 110
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 110 BPM"
    When  8 more measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 110 BPM"
    And   the tempo training header should read "Tempo Training: target reached (110 bpm)"

  @ft:37
  Scenario: Tempo training does not overshoot the target when stepping up
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures and a target of 125
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 125 BPM"

  @ft:38
  Scenario: Tempo training does not overshoot the target when stepping down
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures and a target of 115
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 115 BPM"

  @ft:39
  Scenario: Tempo training holds when BPM already equals the target
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures and a target of 120
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    And   the tempo training header should read "Tempo Training: target reached (120 bpm)"

  @ft:42
  Scenario: Default Start row matches the default BPM while stopped
    Given tempo training is enabled
    Then  the tempo training table's Start row should read "120 bpm"

  @ft:43
  Scenario: Start row mirrors manual BPM changes while stopped
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is stopped
    When  I press "up"
    Then  the tempo training table's Start row should read "121 bpm"

  @ft:44
  Scenario: Start row is captured and held fixed once the metronome starts playing
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is stopped
    And   the tempo training table's Start row reads "120 bpm"
    When  I press "space"
    Then  the tempo training table's Start row should read "120 bpm"

  @ft:54
  Scenario: Start row stays fixed while tempo training steps the BPM away from it
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"
    And   the tempo training table's Start row should still read "120 bpm"

  @ft:55
  Scenario: Start row is re-captured after stopping and restarting at a new BPM
    Given tempo training is enabled
    And   the metronome is playing
    And   the BPM is 130
    And   the tempo training table's Start row should read "130 bpm"
    When  I press "space"
    And   I press "shift+up"
    And   I press "shift+up"
    And   I press "space"
    Then  the tempo training table's Start row should read "150 bpm"

  @ft:58
  Scenario: BPM reverts to the Start value when the metronome stops
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"
    When  I press "space"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    And   the status bar should show "STOPPED"

  @ft:59
  Scenario: Start does not revert to a drifted BPM when the metronome stops
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    And   I press "space"
    Then  the tempo training table's Start row should read "120 bpm"

  @ft:70
  Scenario: Tempo training table is hidden by default
    Then  the tempo training table should not be shown

  @ft:71
  Scenario: Tempo training table appears when turned on
    When  I press "t"
    Then  the tempo training table should be shown

  @ft:56
  Scenario: Tempo training table disappears when turned off
    Given tempo training is enabled
    When  I press "t"
    Then  the tempo training table should not be shown

  @ft:57
  Scenario: Tempo training header is always shown, even while off
    Then  the tempo training header should read "Tempo Training: off"

  @ft:63
  Scenario: Measure counter is hidden when tempo training is off
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  STOPPED"

  @ft:64
  Scenario: Measure counter appears in the status bar once tempo training is on
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the metronome is playing
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  PLAYING  ·  1/8"

  @ft:65
  Scenario: Measure counter increments as measures complete
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  3 measures have elapsed
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  PLAYING  ·  3/8"

  @ft:66
  Scenario: Measure counter holds at the interval value between beat 4 and beat 1
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  PLAYING  ·  8/8"

  @ft:67
  Scenario: Measure counter resets once the pending step lands on beat 1
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    And   beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  PLAYING  ·  1/8"

  @ft:68
  Scenario: Measure counter resets when the metronome stops
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  3 measures have elapsed
    And   I press "space"
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  STOPPED  ·  1/8"

  @ft:72
  Scenario: Measure counter does not advance until beat 1 of the next measure
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  1 measure has elapsed
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  PLAYING  ·  1/8"
    When  beat 1 of the next measure is struck
    Then  the status bar should read "mn  ·  PLAYING  ·  2/8"
